  "scenario_results": [
    "The fixture starts from a BOM/CRLF note and captures its base revision. The note is externally moved to a second path before the stale incoming write.",
    "The stale write reports a revision conflict with no current revision, leaves the original path absent, and leaves the renamed path's original bytes intact.",
    "Incoming editor bytes remain readable in protected conflict history. The journal records conflict state, the original relative path, expected revision, and incoming revision.",
    "The failure-matrix fixture now has executable Rust coverage for six of its eleven scenarios. Five scenarios remain pending."
  ],
